      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "THIS! I wish the radial menu had the option for point-and-click controls, or something not dependent on the extremely inaccurate analog sticks- especially for things like dialing in radial sliders.\n\nYou already kind of can have this sort of control in regards to avatar expressions by adding the expressions menu as a wing to your menu, but for things like avatar/physbone overlay, you still need to use the joystick.\n\nLegitimately almost made me throw my controllers, it was incredibly frustrating. The spatial tracking of the controllers on the quest 2 is far more accurate than the joysticks, and I wish you could use that precision for movement like you would with hand tracking.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-12-29T01:59:27.583Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "My radial menu is becoming nearly unusable because of the increasingly bad stick drift on my index controllers, it would be really nice if I could control the menu by just moving my hand in the desired direction (a la half-life alyx) instead of having to use the joystick",
